    "title": "How To Watch Oscars 2026: Streaming Info, Start Time & Everything You Need To Know",
    "text": "Published Mar 15, 2026, 3:22 PM EDT Dani Kessel Odom (they/them) is an autistic lead writer and TV critic who frequently covers sci-fi shows like Doctor Who and Pluribus, fantasy shows like The Magicians and Percy Jackson, horror, and superheroes. Their specialty is onscreen book adaptations. They have covered events, such as the Denver Fan Expo. Their articles have also been shared by professionals in the field, such as Damien Leone and Lucy Hale. Their review for Ponies was quoted in the show's TV trailer. In university, they majored in English Writing with a minor in psychology. They have always had a passion for analyzing TV and movies, even taking filmography and scriptwriting classes in university. They also studied and participated in onstage and onscreen acting extensively from the ages of 7 to 18. Aside from working at Screen Rant, Dani has worked as a freelance editor and writer over the past decade, often in a ghostwriting capacity. The 2026 Oscars take place tonight, and we have all the streaming information you need to watch the event. The awards season runs from November to March, and the Academy Awards, aka the Oscars, are the most anticipated part of it. The Academy Awards started in 1929, so it’s quickly approaching its 100th anniversary. This year is the 98th, and it's already expected to be a great night. Global phenomena like Sinners, Kpop Demon Hunter, and Weapons are up for awards this year. Plus, more than fifteen actors could get their first Academy Awards at the 2026 Oscars. These stats could help you decide your 2026 Oscar predictions before the event kicks off. If you want to tune in, here is everything you need to know about when and where to watch the 2026 Oscars. The 98th Academy Awards Will Air on ABC & Stream On Hulu The 98th Academy Awards take place on Sunday, March 15, honoring the best movies of 2025 and the incredible talents involved in making them. The event will air on both streaming and cable, giving it a wide reach. Anyone with cable should tune into ABC. Meanwhile, the event will stream live on Hulu. Where The Oscars Are Being Held (& When The Red Carpet Starts) Still courtesy of Warner Bros. The Oscars will take place at the Dolby Theater at Ovation Hollywood in LA. The theater was designed with the Academy Awards in mind. What’s more, they’ve hosted them since 2001, and will continue through 2028. The red carpet always takes place before the Oscars, allowing audiences to see what the celebrities are wearing and get details about their upcoming projects. This portion of the Oscars will start at 6:30 p.m. Eastern Time/3:30 Pacific Time. What Time The 98th Academy Awards Begins The 98th Oscars start at 7 p.m. Eastern time/4 p.m. Pacific time, and they’re expected to run for three and a half hours, not including the red carpet. Who Is Hosting The 98th Academy Awards Ceremony As usual, the awards will be presented by other successful members of the entertainment industry. This year’s awards presenters include, but are not limited to, Sigourney Weaver, Delroy Lindo, and Pedro Pascal. The Biggest Nominations Of Oscars 2026 Explained The 98th Academy Awards nominees all deserve appreciation, even if only one can win in each category. If the past awards shows this season are any indication, the 2026 Oscars will have some fierce competition, and it’s unlikely one movie will sweep all the categories. The biggest competition will be between Warner Bros' One Battle After Another and Sinners. The biggest categories are always Best Picture, Best Actress in a Leading Role, and Best Actor in a Leading Role. All three are tight this year. Although the category has 10 nominees, the movies most likely to win Best Picture are Bugonia, Hamnet, One Battle After Another, Sentimental Value, or Sinners. The actresses nominated for Leading Role are Jessie Buckley for Hamnet, Rose Byrne for If I Had Legs, I’d Kick You, Kate Hudson for Song Sung Blue, Renate Reinsve for Sentimental Value, and Emma Stone for Bugonia. The actors nominated for Leading Role are Timothee Chalamet for Marty Supreme, Leonardo DiCaprio for One Battle After Another, Ethan Hawke for Blue Moon, Michael B. Jordan for Sinners, and Wagner Moura for The Secret Agent. ScreenRant has made our predictions for the Oscar 2026 winners in every category, and we will analyze the biggest moments and award winners of the night. So, check back throughout the night to find out what happened at the 98th Academy Awards.",
